# The same machine, with the buffer told to hold rather than pass.
#
# A trickle of 26 steam a tick is below every turbine's threshold forever. The
# same trickle gathered into 400 and thrown at them is 67 each for two ticks in
# seven, which is over the line -- and a turbine spins up faster than it spins
# down, so it does not quite fall back between pulses. Nothing was added and
# nothing was made bigger. The steam that was being condensed is being used.
#
# This is the one decision in the experiment that nobody guesses first.

machine "Pulsed"

reactor   R1  at 0,0  throttle 20
exchanger HX1 at 4,0
pump      W1  at 0,5
tank      TK1 at 7,0  pulse 400 0

turbine   T1  at 10,0
turbine   T2  at 10,3
turbine   T3  at 10,6

generator G1  at 14,0
generator G2  at 14,3
generator G3  at 14,6

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire HX1.steam -> TK1.in
wire TK1.out -> T1.steam
wire TK1.out -> T2.steam
wire TK1.out -> T3.steam
wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G2.rotary
wire T3.rotary -> G3.rotary
